{
  // The package name, as declared in pubspec.yaml / package.json.
  "name": "gg_quickjs",

  // 1-2 sentence summary about this repo.
  "summary": "QuickJS-ng 0.17.0 for Dart: its C sources and QuickjsNgBuild for the build hooks of native packages, and a Dart binding (JsRuntime, JsIsolateRuntime) with typed values and a closed-by-default sandbox.",

  // 1-3 bullet points: the problem space.
  "domain": [
    "QuickJS-ng sources (core, no quickjs-libc) built as a static library with hidden symbols: package:gg_quickjs/hook.dart, QuickjsNgBuild, quickjsNgVersion, tool/update-quickjs-ng.js",
    "Dart binding: native asset gg_quickjs from the C bridge src/gg_quickjs.{h,c}; JsRuntime (evaluate, modules, bytecode, globals, host functions, futures/promises), JsValue handles, withJsValues, sealed JsException, JsRuntime.spawn -> JsIsolateRuntime",
    "Sandbox and limits: JsRuntimeOptions grants console, timers, fetch (JsNetworkAccess), fs and file imports (JsFileSystemAccess); memoryLimit, timeout, interrupt, maxStackSize, also for conversions"
  ],

  // The repos this one depends on and the repos depending on it.
  // Keep the reason or the API behind each entry, not just the name.
  "interfaces": {
    // "<repo-a>": "why / API"
    "uses": {
      "dna_ggsuite": "dev dependency: the DNA layer with guides, templates, scripts and skills",
      "helix": "dev dependency: the DNA engine that instantiates dna_ggsuite"
    },

    // "<repo-b>": "why / API"
    "usedBy": {}
  }
}
